**Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root before changing code. It is the single
source of these rules.**

This file used to hold its own copy and had already drifted from the other two:
it was the only one of the three stating "PostgreSQL is the fact source, Redis is
cache only" — a locked decision (ADR-0005) that every executor needs, not a
Cursor-specific one. That rule now lives in `AGENTS.md` with the rest.

Repeated here only because they are the ones most often violated, and worth
seeing without opening a second file:

- One task card at a time, from `docs/spec/08-roadmap-ai-ide.md`. Do not pull
  later milestones forward.
- Schema changes go through Flyway. **PostgreSQL is the source of truth; Redis is
  cache, rate limiting and short-lived state only.**
- Validate every LLM output. Cite the original `evidence_passage`, never an
  AI-written summary as final evidence.
- Run the relevant tests and report the results before claiming completion.
